    {
      "id": "Ugy5ZzZRhgurvKcQjeR4AaABAg",
      "author": "@radamicic2740",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_nmsHM9VaMCFDj8G3BfkXbBOy5SzvqZbcIpTMc_lxIQhCo=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "The documentary lost some of the genuine value and authenticity of its content because the original names of cities, towns, regions, traditional foods, and culturally significant words were pronounced as they would be in English.\r\n\r\nNames such as Subotica, Kragujevac, Leskovac, Šumadija, Vranje, as well as cultural words such as rakija, kajmak, ajvar, and porodica, carry a sense of place, history, and identity. Their pronunciation is an important part of preserving their meaning and cultural character.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, the narrator did not make the effort to pronounce these important words in their original form. Even a small amount of attention to authentic pronunciation would have made the documentary feel more respectful, genuine, and connected to the culture it was presenting.                                                    Had to stop watching!",
      "likeCount": 0,
