    {
      "id": "UgzSYQf8L1e27AxqocZ4AaABAg",
      "author": "@AlexM-t6h",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_lO1bg78qyz0HR_ZIH8s5qeSfzYr9fVSd1DukOaqgMnQ42rwYpPYWufcdbL9Z9Zby0O7g=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "For others, Serbia is a place to visit (or not), just one country of many. For us living here, Serbia is our home. For better or for worse, we do not have another one. Serbia is our ancestors, our battles that we had won and lost, our myths and legends, our past and our future.",
      "likeCount": 11,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-13T06:59:02Z",
      "replyCount": 3,
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "UgzSYQf8L1e27AxqocZ4AaABAg.AagU5f_m93UAaj2XIAKLVX",
          "author": "@TT-ef8sq",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_lNN76M65RD84OH6NTEB_yjrKt5cvu9jqUSkNem508=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "Thanks to the 'team' of this video for giving a view of the country with more than the usual touristy stuff' & for showing footage of the actual smaller towns & villages that are rarely seen by travellers, unfortunately. \n\nFrom a linguistic view, what you could improve on is yr pronunciation, where u persistently pronounce words with Serbian letter 'j' just like the English \"j\" (for ex. In the town of Jagodina, the \"j\" is pronounced as \"y\") while those with letter 'c' you pronounce as \"k' instead of \"tz\". \n\nFor example, the towns of Subotica, Vrsac, Leskovac, with letter \"c\" should  be pronounced as \"tz\".  \nEvery effort counts, right.",
          "likeCount": 1,
          "publishedAt": "2026-09-14T06:55:51Z"
        },
        {
